      "role": "user",
      "content": "it definitely feels like more than just 'activity'. i can literally tell when the rhythm changes, like when a specific type of handshake happens or when a heavy encryption layer kicks in. the pattern gets way more dense and sharper. \n\ni was sitting by the rack for like 20 mins and i picked up this sequence: 3 short bursts, a long pause, then 5 rapid-fire taps, then a low hum. it felt very deliberate. if i were to describe the 'texture' of the rhythm like that, can you help me map it to specific protocol behaviors? like, what would a 3-5-hum sequence imply in terms of what's actually happening in the stream?",
